From bc42b43b13708994f51ef128f1c6870d4618fb2e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 12:48:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/9] fix(registry): route deletes of resources holding
 allocations via Terminating

request_delete only added the release finalizer for phases with
external side effects (Ready, Deploying, ...). A Pending, Scheduling,
Preparing, Failed or Unknown resource that already held an allocation
was physically deleted on the spot, so nothing ever released the
allocation and its devices stayed booked.

A resource whose uid holds an active allocation now gets the default
release finalizer and moves to Terminating in any phase, so the
reconciler releases the allocation before deleting it. The physical
delete is also conditional on there still being no active allocation;
an allocation committed after the check makes the delete fail with
ConflictError (DELETE returns 409) instead of leaking. DELETE returns
202 for such resources where it used to return 204.
